Fix Lua `require()` for modules in the top-level script directory (e.g. `Data/`)

PoB v2.66.0+ added `require("Data.StatDescriptions.stat_descriptions")` in
`src/Classes/TradeHelpers.lua`. The RPOB host only registers
`${script_dir}/lua/?.lua` on `package.path`, so requires of modules that live
at the top level of the script directory (like `Data/...`) can never resolve.
Register the script dir itself as well, mirroring the original PoB host
behavior.

In 0.3.3 the Lua setup moved from `src/lua.rs` (register_package_paths) to
`src/pob.rs` (create_lua / util::append_lua_package_dir), so this version of
the patch targets that new call site.

diff --git a/src/pob.rs b/src/pob.rs
--- a/src/pob.rs
+++ b/src/pob.rs
@@ -111,6 +111,9 @@ impl PathOfBuilding {
         // `unsafe_new` needed to allow loading of C modules
         let lua = unsafe { Lua::unsafe_new() };
         append_lua_package_dir(&lua, &ctx.script_dir.join("lua"))?;
+        // PoB 2.66+ requires modules from the top-level script directory
+        // (e.g. `Data.StatDescriptions.stat_descriptions`), not just `lua/`.
+        append_lua_package_dir(&lua, &ctx.script_dir)?;
 
         // expose import url to lua
         let args = Args::parse();
